exit: 1
-- SYNTAX ------------------- errors/parse_error_19.march

A function's return type comes after a colon, `: Int`, not an arrow `-> Int`: [parse_error]

3 |   fn f(x: Int, y: Int) -> Int do
                           ^

    fn name(x : Int) : Int do
        ...
    end

    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

3 -   fn f(x: Int, y: Int) -> Int do
3 +   fn f(x: Int, y: Int) : Int do

    run `march --explain parse_error`

after fix: exit 0
